      "content": "I understand that the well-meaning advice to \"cope better\" can feel dismissive of the profound, deep damage you are describing. It is often not about \"patching a wound,\" but more about how to build a life *around the reality of the damage you have sustained\n\nWhen the \"self\" feels gone, the focus can sometimes shift from \"fixing the self\" to **gently finding a way to guide the present self that is here now\n\nPlease consider that self-compassion, not self-reconstruction, can be the first, and most vital, step in this process",
      "source": "target",
